    "body": "## Description\n\nThis PR allows `max-connections` to work with a bare `unix` address in `-ipcbind`.\n\nPreviously, `unix,max-connections=8` was rejected, while `unix:,max-connections=8` worked.\n\nThis change makes both formats valid and consistent, making the option easier to use and avoiding unnecessary configuration errors.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added unit tests in `ipc_tests.cpp`. The tests pass with the fix and fail without it.\n- Tested `-ipcbind=unix,max-connections=8` on regtest and confirmed that it creates 8 connection slots.\n\n## Help text\n\nThe original help text now works as written, so the proposed help text change was removed.\n\nFixes #36657\n",
